# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Documentation / handoff (NOT tracked — internal notes, handoff files, specs)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
docs/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets & sanitization (public repo — never commit these)
# Each subproject .gitignore duplicates this privacy block on purpose:
# belt and suspenders. Keep them in sync when editing here.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Environment / config — ALL env files are ignored; only *.example templates are tracked
*.env
*.env.*
!*.env.example
*.local

# Private keys, mnemonics, wallets, keystores
*.pem
*.key
*.keystore
*.p12
*.pfx
*.pw
key/
keys/
keystore/
keystores/
wallets/
*mnemonic*
*seed-phrase*
*private-key*
*privatekey*
secrets/
.secret
.secrets
.foundry/

# Cloud / API credentials
.aws/
credentials.json
service-account*.json

# Bead photos never touch git (EXIF = location leak) — all image formats banned
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.png
*.gif
*.bmp
*.tif
*.tiff
*.webp
*.heic
*.heif
*.avif
*.raw
*.dng

# Exception: generated brand raster assets (favicons, token images, OG image)
# in the Astro public/ folder — build output, never a bead photo, never has EXIF.
#
# Enumerated deliberately rather than globbed. site/public/ is the web-servable
# folder, so it is exactly where a jar photo would plausibly be dropped later;
# a blanket !/site/public/*.png would silently un-ban it. These names are the
# complete output set of brand/build.mjs — if that script gains an output, you
# must add it here too. Nothing will warn you if you forget: git add skips
# ignored files silently, and the build has no way to know what git did.
!/site/public/favicon-16x16.png
!/site/public/favicon-32x32.png
!/site/public/apple-touch-icon.png
!/site/public/android-chrome-192x192.png
!/site/public/android-chrome-512x512.png
!/site/public/beadz-token-256.png
!/site/public/beadz-token-512.png
!/site/public/og-image.png

